<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00576">
	<title>Forward Attention Warning malfunction</title>
	<conbody>
		<table frame="none" colsep="1" rowsep="1" outputclass="formatc_none" id="e03681">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1" outputclass="FormatA">
				<colspec colnum="1" colname="1" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colnum="2" colname="2" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="0">
						<entry colname="1" colsep="0">
							<fig id="e03682">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="images/N_QVe27_C00_142_E.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="2">
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e03683">
								<li>
									<p><uicontrol>Check the in-cabin monitoring system.</uicontrol></p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>When Forward Attention Warning is not working properly, the warning message appears on the instrument cluster for several seconds, the Forward attention warning light (<image href="images/WKIA_353.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>) and the Master warning light (<image href="images/WKIA_040.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>) light up on the instrument cluster, and an audible warning sounds once. If this occurs, have your vehicle inspected by a professional workshop. Kia recommends visiting an authorized Kia dealer or service partner.</p>
	</conbody>
